      "side": 1,
      "message": "Another thing that struck me this morning: While KMI breaking changes can be merged in -kminext, they are not supposed to be build-breaking changes. Since this changes function signatures and ops function-pointers, it seems possible this may cause build issues with vendor/oem driver implementations.\n\nAgain, I\u0027m not super familiar with fuse code, so I\u0027m not sure exactly how externally impacting this change would be. SandeepD would probably have a better insight.\n\nIf this change could be reworked in a fashion suggested here: https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/kernel/common/+/4194937/comments/182a9036_c6d9393c\n\nWhere we don\u0027t propagate passing the sync flag through so much stuff, it might be better overall.",
